# Charming Prince, third mode: "Exile another target creature you own" - the creature need only be owned, not controlled, by its controller's
# opponent (CR 108.3, 115.1). Bot2 takes Bot1's Savannah Lions with Control Magic on turn 2; on turn 3 the Prince exiles it (Control
# Magic goes to Bot2's graveyard, CR 704.5m), and at the beginning of the next end step the Lions returns under Bot1's control (CR 603.7).
# It is a new object, Bot2 does not get it back. It is the only legal target (the Prince is not another creature), so it is chosen without a prompt.

